# Netlify redirects.
# Docs: https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# The publish directory is the repo root, so every committed file is served
# unless a rule shadows it. Netlify matches static files BEFORE redirect
# rules, so shadowing a file that actually exists requires the force flag
# (the "!" after the status code). Without it these rules are silently
# ignored and the file is served as normal.

